  "query_preview": "..\n(Sunday night through Friday)\nIssued at 235 AM EDT Sat Oct 31 2026\n\nPicking up the forecast Monday morning, a few remnant clearing \nshowers may be in the cards. However, the wedge will remain strong \nwith reinforced flow from the high to the northeast. The next chance \nfor rain comes mid-week. A much more robust trough will clear the \nrockies, bringing widespread rain and thunderstorm across the CONUS. \nThe main forcing from the system will likely remain well to the \nnorth (across the Northern Plains and Great Lakes). This will likely \nmean the precip mode will be reliant on how much it has to fight \nagainst suppressive forcing from the high to the northeast and more \nbroad isentropic lift around and over the wedge. Model spread \nremains high on timing and cohesiveness of the precip. The \nunanswered question will be if the cold front remains cohesive or if \na broader shield of rain develops.\n\nTemperatures through the period will fairly consistent due to \nincreased moisture. Highs will be in the 60s and 70s with remain \nmostly in the 50s to around 60.",
